WEBVTT

00:03:29.579 --> 00:03:32.371
The UDC still exists and defends
Confederate symbols

00:03:32.371 --> 00:03:35.746
as part of a noble heritage of sacrifice
by their ancestors.

00:03:36.246 --> 00:03:37.913
Despite the wealth of primary sources

00:03:37.913 --> 00:03:40.829
showing that slavery was the root cause 
of the Civil War,

00:03:40.829 --> 00:03:43.329
the myth about states’ rights 
persists today.

00:03:43.913 --> 00:03:45.663
In the aftermath of the war,

00:03:45.663 --> 00:03:48.871
Frederick Douglass 
and his abolitionist contemporaries

00:03:48.871 --> 00:03:52.246
feared this erasure of slavery 
from the history of the Civil War

00:03:52.246 --> 00:03:54.038
could contribute 
to the government’s failure

00:03:54.038 --> 00:03:56.329
to protect the rights of Black Americans—

00:03:56.329 --> 00:03:58.788
a fear that has repeatedly
been proven valid.

